    "article_content_rzUTmg": {
      "type": "article__content",
      "blocks": {
        "image_text_3LKP7f": {
          "type": "image_text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-md",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-lg",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-0",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-xl",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "180ch",
            "color": "text-blue",
            "title": "Understandingwildfire smoke",
            "title_style": "h4",
            "richtext": "<p>According to Climate Central, “Wildfires burning within 50-100 miles of a city routinely caused air quality to be 5-15 times worse than normal. Smoke generated by forest fires is comprised of water vapor, particulate matter and a variety of gases, including formaldehyde, benzene, toluene, carbon dioxide, sulfur dioxide, nitrogen oxide, carbon monoxide, and volatile organic compounds (VOCs).\"<\/p><p>These materials each fall into one of two different groups of pollutants: particles or gases. Each group requires a different method of filtration to successfully remove it from the air.<\/p><p>Smoke particles: Largest component and most harmful Fine (PM 2.5). Gas : Nitrogen dioxide, sulfur dioxide, formaldehyde, benzene, toluene<\/p><p>As stated by the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA), “Fine particles...particles generally 2.5 µm in diameter or smaller represent a main pollutant emitted from wildfire smoke.. [and] are [the] greatest health concern. This group of particles also includes ultra fine particles, which are generally classified as having diameters less than 0.1 µm.\"<\/p>",
            "image_mobile": "shopify:\/\/shop_images\/smokemob.png",
            "image_desktop": "shopify:\/\/shop_images\/smoke.webp",
            "image_placement_mobile": "flex-col",
            "image_placement_desktop": "tabletl:flex-row-reverse"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "image_text_3LKP7f"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
